3096, 321, 7331, 11, 321, 279, 15721, 3364, 314, 8009, 7975, 13, 4213, 11, 567, 16739, 21542, 279, 80248, 314, 3992, 8559, 3401, 364, 30557, 11, 11352, 279, 39846, 314, 15352, 40410, 321, 7017, 2730, 2373, 13, 1061, 80248, 369, 41565, 2574, 279, 28810, 1144, 364, 1680, 3401, 13, 271, 760, 6222, 668, 2962, 310, 1761, 2528, 310, 7017, 321, 40410, 2730, 2373, 364, 30557, 314, 7017, 8897, 2094, 279, 1814, 11, 430, 411, 369, 7326, 310, 866, 21333, 47026, 20566, 1114, 5313, 13, 1165, 6922, 10839, 310, 4483, 4473, 7123, 310, 10752, 804, 11813, 321, 36881, 13, 1061, 10616, 369, 264, 40793, 11, 694, 424, 1503, 524, 34795, 279, 12263, 9272, 539, 6575, 18576, 11, 1680, 430, 41228, 220, 16, 24, 314, 10616, 220, 17, 16, 15, 21, 318, 17, 15, 16, 18, 8, 321, 220, 16, 15, 314, 10616, 220, 16, 23, 23, 24, 318, 17, 15, 15, 24, 681, 864, 567, 69554, 2760, 13, 1165, 668, 10000, 1004, 13789, 14713, 310, 21449, 1439, 3087, 303, 279, 7977, 8801, 321, 975, 6434, 12497, 13, 248046], "output_raw": "On behalf of the United Kingdom, I extend congratulations to Germany for the successful adoption of resolution 2467 (2019). While I attach myself to the achievements highlighted by my French colleague, I must also acknowledge the significant steps remaining to ensure survivors are truly at the heart of our approach. The resolution recognizes a survivor-centred approach, the disproportionate impact of conflict-related sexual violence on women and girls, and the vital role of civil society. However, we deeply regret the omission of language regarding services for survivors, specifically the exclusion of comprehensive reproductive and sexual health care. This omission is unacceptable given the acute need for such services.\n\nThe UK will continue to support access to sexual and reproductive health care for survivors of sexual violence around the world, as this is essential to any genuine survivor-centred approach. We remain committed to taking further steps to achieve true justice and accountability. This resolution is a milestone, but it does not erase the framework established by earlier provisions, such as paragraphs 19 of resolution 2106 (2013) and 10 of resolution 1889 (2009), which we reaffirm. We will maintain our ongoing commitment to promoting these rights in the Security Council and other UN bodies.<|im_end|>", "output_display": "On behalf of the United Kingdom, I extend congratulations to Germany for the successful adoption of resolution 2467 (2019). While I attach myself to the achievements highlighted by my French colleague, I must also acknowledge the significant steps remaining to ensure survivors are truly at the heart of our approach. The resolution recognizes a survivor-centred approach, the disproportionate impact of conflict-related sexual violence on women and girls, and the vital role of civil society. However, we deeply regret the omission of language regarding services for survivors, specifically the exclusion of comprehensive reproductive and sexual health care. This omission is unacceptable given the acute need for such services.\n\nThe UK will continue to support access to sexual and reproductive health care for survivors of sexual violence around the world, as this is essential to any genuine survivor-centred approach. We remain committed to taking further steps to achieve true justice and accountability. This resolution is a milestone, but it does not erase the framework established by earlier provisions, such as paragraphs 19 of resolution 2106 (2013) and 10 of resolution 1889 (2009), which we reaffirm. We will maintain our ongoing commitment to promoting these rights in the Security Council and other UN bodies.", "generated_tokens": 257, "generation_seconds": 5.125233991071582, "at_cap": false}
